        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Task Refs & Cancellation",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Save every task in a ==set==: the loop only holds **weak** refs",
            "`add_done_callback(tasks.discard)` frees the ref when it finishes",
            "`task.cancel()` raises `CancelledError` at its next `await`",
            "`TaskGroup` (3.11+) keeps refs for you: ==preferred=="
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def job():",
            "    try:",
            "        await work()",
            "    except asyncio.CancelledError:",
            "        await cleanup()",
            "        raise  # never swallow"
          ],
          "note": "swallowing it means cancel() does nothing"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. TaskGroup Fan-Out",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "  async with TaskGroup() as tg:",
            "    tg.create_task(a())",
            "    tg.create_task(b())",
            "except* ValueError as eg:",
            "  log(eg.exceptions)"
          ],
          "note": "one fails → siblings cancelled"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Block exits only when **all** child tasks finish",
            "One failure cancels the rest: ==no orphaned tasks==",
            "`gather` instead lets siblings **keep running** after an error",
            "Handle each error type with `except*` (3.11+)"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "  async with asyncio.timeout(5):",
            "    async with TaskGroup() as tg:",
            "      tg.create_task(a())",
            "except TimeoutError:",
            "  log('too slow')  # all cancelled"
          ],
          "note": "prefer timeout() to wait_for"
        },
