      "page_title": "Structured Concurrency: Nurseries & Cancel Scopes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. What Is It",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Structured concurrency==: every task lives inside a lexical scope that **can't** exit until all its child tasks finish.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def main():",
            "    async with trio.open_nursery() as n:",
            "        n.start_soon(fetch, 'a')",
            "        n.start_soon(fetch, 'b')",
            "    # reached only when BOTH finish",
            "trio.run(main)"
          ],
          "note": "block waits for all its children"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism: Failure",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One child raises → its ==siblings are cancelled==",
            "All errors surface **together** as an `ExceptionGroup`",
            "Handle each type with `except*` (3.11+)"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "    trio.run(main)",
            "except* ValueError as eg:",
            "    log(eg.exceptions)  # all of them"
          ],
          "note": "except* needs Python 3.11+"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Cancel Scopes",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
