      "page_title": "Sync ↔ Async Bridges: Calls, Offloading & Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Mechanism: The Bridges"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Call",
            "Runs on"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "sync fn from async",
              "`to_thread(fn,*a)`",
              "default pool"
            ],
            [
              "sync fn, own pool",
              "`run_in_executor`",
              "given executor"
            ],
            [
              "coro from a thread",
              "`run_coroutine_threadsafe`",
              "loop → ==cf.Future=="
            ],
            [
              "callback from a thread",
              "`call_soon_threadsafe`",
              "loop thread"
            ],
            [
              "anyio worker → loop",
              "`from_thread.run(fn)`",
              "loop thread"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==to_thread== (3.9+) uses the default pool and **copies** contextvars",
            "`run_in_executor` takes positional args only, so wrap kwargs in `functools.partial`",
            "`call_soon_threadsafe(cb)` is the __only__ safe way for a thread to touch the loop",
            "`anyio.from_thread.run(async_fn)` lets a worker thread call back into the loop"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Example: Offload & Call Back"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
